        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "8048ddc2-cc47-5b0e-8f47-8582077f3b6a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Damian Green\n- Organizations: UK Border Agency, Parliament of the United Kingdom\n- Systems: e-Borders\n- Concepts: free movement, Parliamentary privilege, super-injunctions\n- Events: arrest of Damian Green, calls to reform privilege law\n\nFacts:\n- Due to European law on free movement, EU carriers and ports supplied information to the UK Border Agency for e-Borders on a voluntary basis.\n- Damian Green was born on 17 January 1956.\n- Damian Green has been the Conservative Member of Parliament for Ashford since 1997.\n- In March 2012, Damian Green said that by April e-Borders would be collecting information on all passengers on 100% of non-EEA flights to the UK.\n- In recent years, Parliamentary privilege in the United Kingdom made headlines in relation to the arrest of Damian Green.\n- In recent years, Parliamentary privilege in the United Kingdom also made headlines because of super-injunction cases including \"RJW & SJW v The Guardian newspaper & Person or Persons Unknown\" and \"CTB v News Group Newspapers,\" leading to calls to reform the law relating to privilege.\n- Damian Green became First Secretary of State and Minister for the Cabinet Office on 11 June 2017.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "87ab5433-890f-5969-bc67-37494ff06ee6",
        "text": "Page: E-Borders. Sentence: Due to European law on free movement EU carriers and ports supply information to the UK Border Agency on a voluntary basis, however in March 2012 Damian Green said that by April e-Borders would be collecting information an all passengers on 100% of non-EEA flights to the UK.\nPage: Damian Green. Sentence: Damian Howard Green (born 17 January 1956) is a British politician who has been the Conservative Member of Parliament for Ashford since 1997 and the First Secretary of State and Minister for the Cabinet Office since 11 June 2017.\nPage: Parliamentary privilege in the United Kingdom. Sentence: In recent years the doctrine of Parliamentary privilege has made headlines in relation to the arrest of Damian Green and several cases relating to super-injunctions such as \"RJW & SJW v The Guardian newspaper & Person or Persons Unknown\" ('Trafigura') and \"CTB v News Group Newspapers\" leading to calls to reform the law relating to privilege.",
